{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nEvery COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar is emitted with `material=None` — `completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)` at `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:405`, with the comment at `:754` noting no fingerprint is computed on this path. Measured on the live store: 0 of the most recent 300 COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (216 PASS / 59 FAIL / 23 no-verdict / 2 ERROR) carry any material/material_fingerprint field.\n\n## Consequence (why this is worth fixing)\n\nA FAIL followed by a PASS on the same `verified_at_sha` cannot be attributed: verifier inputs include ticket comments and prefetched evidence, which change without a code commit, so \"no commit in between\" does not mean \"same inputs.\" This makes the completion gate's precision unmeasurable from its own records (an analysis this week mis-derived an \"80–84% FP\" figure from exactly this gap), and it means completion attestations cannot support the stale-material currency discipline that plan-review attestations already have.\n\nNote: the `material=None` is deliberate per the code's own comment — this ticket treats the capability gap as the defect (operator-directed filing, 2026-08-31). Formula/prompt version stamping in the same record would make longitudinal gate analysis version-aware (pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time, so unversioned sidecars conflate formula eras).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (PASS, FAIL, ERROR alike) record a material fingerprint over the verifier's actual inputs (ticket material as pinned for the run: description/ACs/comments snapshot + evidence set identifiers), reusing the existing plan-review fingerprint machinery where applicable rather than inventing a new scheme.\n- [ ] Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint.\n- [ ] Existing sidecars are untouched (no backfill); consumers treat absent material as \"unknown era\".\n- [ ] A regression test asserts a FAIL sidecar carries a non-null fingerprint and version.\n\n## File impact\n\nTo be confirmed at investigation (bugs do not pre-declare impact): expected `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` (or equivalent emitter), one test module.\n\n## Fix plan (2026-08-31, concise reviewed scope)\n\nRoot cause: completion verifier results already carry or can carry input identity, but `completion_sidecar.build_payload` only serializes the explicit `material` argument. Close-time and standalone emitters pass `material=None`, atomic PASS calls `build_payload` directly, and completion `gate_error_v1` records lack the same version/fingerprint observability. The change is additive record enrichment only: verdicts, close blocking, signing eligibility, and best-effort error swallowing must not change.\n\nFingerprint contract: new sidecars keep `material_fingerprint`, as sha256-16 over JSON schema `completion_verifier_material_v1`.\n\nNormal pinned PASS/FAIL writes `material_basis=\"pinned_completion_inputs\"` and hashes: existing plan-review material fingerprint (`current_material_fingerprint` / `pass1.material_fingerprint`), pinned `completion_read_basis` identifiers (`code_oid`, `tickets_oid`, `receipt_digest`, `run_id`), and `completion_prefetch_manifest` identifiers (`path`, `mode`) threaded from the precheck's `PRE-LOAD MANIFEST`. Example basis keys: `{schema, material_basis, plan_material_fingerprint, completion_read_basis:{code_oid,tickets_oid,receipt_digest,run_id}, completion_prefetch_manifest:[{path,mode}]}`. `receipt_digest` is load-bearing because it covers the exact ticket/comments snapshot.\n\nFallbacks are explicit: `material_basis=\"unpinned_completion_inputs\"` for legacy/local/deterministic precheck FAIL with current plan material but no read basis; `material_basis=\"error_unpinned\"` for completion ERROR before a verdict result exists. If no ticket material can be read, material remains absent/unknown and the gate outcome is unchanged.\n\nVersion contract: every new completion sidecar carries `verifier_version={prompt_id:\"completion-verifier\", prompt_content_sha256:\"<git-canonical prompt hash>\", formula_version:\"<signing.gate_code_version()>\"}`. This reuses existing prompt-library and gate-code-version machinery; old records without it remain unknown era.\n\nShared ERROR scope: `gate_error_sidecar` serves plan_review, code_review, and completion. Enrichment is conditional on `gate == \"completion\"` only. Completion ERROR call sites covered: `produce_completion_verdict` preflight and `completion_failures.raise_completion_workflow_failure`. Plan-review/code-review ERROR shapes stay unchanged.\n\nFile impact: `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py`; `src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py`; `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py`; `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/completion-verification.yaml`; `src/rebar/schemas/completion_precheck_output.schema.json`; `src/rebar/schemas/completion_reconcile_input.schema.json`; `src/rebar/llm/gate_error_sidecar.py`; `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py`.\n\nVerification: (1) RED first: add a FAIL-sidecar regression test and run only it; it fails today because `material_fingerprint` is null and `verifier_version` absent. (2) GREEN: tests assert pinned FAIL has non-null version, `material_basis=\"pinned_completion_inputs\"`, includes prefetch manifest, and its fingerprint changes when `receipt_digest` changes; also cover PASS direct-builder enrichment, unpinned FAIL fallback, completion-only ERROR enrichment, and plan/code-review ERROR non-enrichment. (3) AC3 reader proof: `latest_fail_verdict` / `latest_pass_record` still return legacy records lacking material/version. (4) Mutation-teeth in sandbox: reintroduce the builder omission; held-out FAIL test returns RED, then restore. (5) Focused sidecar/workflow/atomic-close tests plus lint/typecheck.\n\nAC mapping: AC1 pinned PASS/FAIL fingerprint includes existing plan material, receipt digest, and prefetch identifiers; fallback values mark unpinned/error cases. AC2 is `verifier_version`. AC3 has no backfill/prune/reader rejection change. AC4 is the RED→GREEN FAIL test, including receipt-digest dependency.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788235390199536001,"uuid":"29ee07ab-a599-453d-bfea-71c45b93641f"}